WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:19.045
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:19.315 --> 00:20.801
Hey, yo!

3
00:30.470 --> 00:31.550
I’ve got something for you.

4
00:37.676 --> 00:38.756
Why is there so much money?

5
00:38.928 --> 00:40.143
I got a new job.

6
00:40.417 --> 00:43.257
It’s at a convenience store. Easy work, good pay.

7
00:43.450 --> 00:44.730
You don’t have to worry anymore.

8
00:46.362 --> 00:48.242
You’ll finally have money to go back to school.

9
00:50.542 --> 00:51.982
Who said I was going back to school?

10
00:52.086 --> 00:54.399
I have to work too, so we can help each other.

11
00:56.193 --> 00:57.646
I don’t need your help.

12
00:58.011 --> 01:00.424
I can take care of my little sister.

13
01:02.192 --> 01:04.455
Besides, I won’t be some low-level employee forever.

14
01:04.702 --> 01:06.370
I’m going to rise all the way to

15
01:06.511 --> 01:07.527
store owner.

16
01:08.351 --> 01:09.750
Wow, look at you.

17
01:10.119 --> 01:11.119
Big talk!

18
01:12.950 --> 01:13.260
Huh?

19
01:13.315 --> 01:14.494
What? What?

20
01:14.756 --> 01:15.246
Come on.

21
01:15.293 --> 01:17.413
You don’t even know if you’ll survive as an employee.

22
01:18.266 --> 01:19.973
Come on, let’s practice.

23
01:21.351 --> 01:23.584
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

24
02:47.941 --> 02:50.270
Wow, where have you been?

25
02:50.547 --> 02:52.000
You’re back late.

26
02:52.658 --> 02:54.428
Look, it’s almost eight.

27
02:58.396 --> 03:00.613
Nava was hungry.

28
03:00.699 --> 03:02.343
There was nothing in the fridge,

29
03:02.783 --> 03:04.763
so I fried her some eggs.

30
03:06.323 --> 03:08.143
Thank you for looking after Nava.

31
03:12.637 --> 03:13.637
Come on.

32
03:13.746 --> 03:15.823
It’s nothing. It was no trouble.

33
03:16.359 --> 03:19.704
But next time you’re going to be late, give me a call.

34
03:19.852 --> 03:20.852
It’s all right.

35
03:21.453 --> 03:23.080
I probably won’t need to trouble you again.

36
03:23.104 --> 03:24.516
Why not?

37
03:25.084 --> 03:26.384
Is the job no good?

38
03:38.320 --> 03:39.414
He chanted every day.

39
03:40.447 --> 03:41.880
But it was no use.

40
03:43.369 --> 03:45.883
I kept telling him to follow the rules.

41
03:46.470 --> 03:50.403
Now I have to recruit a new night-shift employee again.

42
03:56.390 --> 03:57.430
What on earth is going on?

43
03:59.737 --> 04:00.765
Is Bird really dead?

44
04:05.023 --> 04:06.023
Cherd.

45
04:06.289 --> 04:08.526
I’ve already thrown Bird’s hand out behind the store.

46
04:09.007 --> 04:10.007
Okay.

47
04:10.596 --> 04:11.167
Here.

48
04:11.550 --> 04:12.792
I’ll throw it away.

49
04:13.537 --> 04:14.575
Thank you so much, Dear.

50
04:15.951 --> 04:20.108
I think we should clean up these bloodstains.

51
04:21.255 --> 04:23.255
That should take us right to the end of the shift.

52
04:24.552 --> 04:25.552
Hey.

53
04:26.570 --> 04:28.157
Have you people lost your minds?

54
04:30.603 --> 04:31.686
A man died!

55
04:36.150 --> 04:37.150
I’m calling the police.

56
04:39.283 --> 04:40.283
Wait.

57
04:43.203 --> 04:44.923
You said you were going to call the police.

58
04:45.556 --> 04:46.836
What are you going to tell them?

59
04:47.364 --> 04:49.596
“My coworker was killed by a ghost.

60
04:50.463 --> 04:52.050
A ghost ate him alive.

61
04:52.075 --> 04:53.355
All that was left was his hand.”

62
04:54.430 --> 04:55.710
Do you think they’d believe you?

63
04:57.477 --> 04:58.477
Mr. Metha.

64
04:59.743 --> 05:01.357
You used to be a police officer, too.

65
05:02.563 --> 05:03.597
You know...

66
05:04.375 --> 05:07.155
If you tell them what really happened tonight,

67
05:08.095 --> 05:09.642
you know what will happen.

68
05:12.416 --> 05:13.416
I...

69
05:16.143 --> 05:17.143
You...

70
05:18.117 --> 05:19.117
Dear...

71
05:19.950 --> 05:21.650
We will all become suspects.

72
05:23.219 --> 05:24.766
That’s right.

73
05:26.273 --> 05:27.539
You know it.

74
05:33.316 --> 05:35.123
Then what was the thing that ate Bird?

75
05:35.776 --> 05:37.023
A customer.

76
05:37.773 --> 05:38.973
I told you from the beginning.

77
05:40.159 --> 05:41.466
But don’t worry.

78
05:42.059 --> 05:43.183
Customers like that

79
05:43.498 --> 05:45.176
only show up after midnight.

80
05:45.856 --> 05:46.856
During the day,

81
05:46.921 --> 05:47.921
they’re harmless.

82
05:47.960 --> 05:49.393
They never show themselves.

83
05:50.366 --> 05:51.505
So you mean...

84
05:51.685 --> 05:53.605
we have to risk our lives like this every night?

85
05:55.190 --> 05:56.691
Now you can see

86
05:57.623 --> 05:59.356
why a convenience store job

87
06:00.096 --> 06:02.115
pays so much.

88
06:15.843 --> 06:16.843
Then I quit.

89
06:17.523 --> 06:18.523
Hey!

90
06:18.982 --> 06:19.775
You quit?

91
06:19.799 --> 06:21.548
I can’t take this every night.

92
06:21.915 --> 06:24.462
Think it over first. It’s just a job.

93
06:26.723 --> 06:27.723
Seriously.

94
06:28.348 --> 06:29.348
You...

95
06:30.056 --> 06:31.816
You’re the most promising employee I’ve seen

96
06:32.136 --> 06:33.476
since I started working here.

97
06:38.503 --> 06:39.503
Here, Dear.

98
06:39.541 --> 06:40.292
10,000.

99
06:40.549 --> 06:41.549
Thank you.

100
06:45.096 --> 06:46.096
This money

101
06:46.743 --> 06:47.743
is for tonight.

102
06:49.198 --> 06:50.718
Count it and make sure it’s all there.

103
07:01.954 --> 07:04.471
Dear, get rid of that for me, then wipe up the blood.

104
07:04.496 --> 07:05.501
Okay, Cherd.

105
07:25.525 --> 07:26.525
Teacher!

106
07:30.570 --> 07:31.585
Study hard, Nava.

107
07:33.190 --> 07:34.630
I’ll pick you up this evening.

108
07:44.926 --> 07:45.926
Hello.

109
07:52.143 --> 07:53.450
Have you lost weight?

110
07:55.596 --> 07:56.805
I’m fine, Mom.

111
07:59.386 --> 08:00.959
How are Nam and Nava?

112
08:01.310 --> 08:02.310
Did they come with you?

113
08:03.479 --> 08:04.537
Nam...

114
08:06.332 --> 08:07.525
She is at work right now.

115
08:08.523 --> 08:11.413
Nava’s at school, so they couldn’t come.

116
08:15.943 --> 08:16.943
And...

117
08:17.483 --> 08:19.136
don’t you have to go to work?

118
08:19.536 --> 08:21.650
I’m on the night shift today, Mom.

119
08:24.776 --> 08:25.776
And when...

120
08:26.303 --> 08:28.516
will you finally get promoted to inspector?

121
08:31.862 --> 08:32.902
Probably not much longer.

122
08:34.097 --> 08:35.097
Because...

123
08:35.599 --> 08:37.210
I just closed a case recently.

124
08:40.586 --> 08:42.099
Good job, son.

125
08:44.493 --> 08:47.346
Next time you visit, wear your uniform, okay?

126
08:48.416 --> 08:49.416
I want to see it.

127
08:51.096 --> 08:52.096
Okay.

128
08:59.797 --> 09:00.797
Mom.

129
09:02.090 --> 09:03.543
Aren’t you hungry?

130
09:04.531 --> 09:06.785
The caregiver said you haven’t been eating anything.

131
09:08.248 --> 09:09.350
Please eat something.

132
09:16.809 --> 09:17.943
Mom.

133
09:19.848 --> 09:20.848
Mom.

134
09:24.607 --> 09:25.607
Mom.

135
09:28.529 --> 09:29.530
Mom!

136
09:32.660 --> 09:33.605
I’m sorry.

137
09:33.630 --> 09:34.630
Mom.

138
09:35.461 --> 09:38.156
I was wrong. I was wrong.

139
09:39.643 --> 09:41.136
I was wrong.

140
09:41.501 --> 09:43.356
Could you please wait outside for a moment?

141
09:44.496 --> 09:45.628
Ms. Phen?

142
09:46.590 --> 09:47.590
Please step outside.

143
09:49.153 --> 09:50.153
Please calm down.

144
10:04.799 --> 10:06.356
(Job Application - Accountant Dear HR, Job Application-Sales Executive)

145
10:06.380 --> 10:08.000
(Job Application - Human Resources (HR), Administrative Staff (Admin))

146
10:08.024 --> 10:09.803
(Dear HR Department, I would like to submit my resume to apply for the Accountant position.)

147
10:09.827 --> 10:11.787
(I am highly interested in joining your company.)

148
10:50.825 --> 10:52.794
Hey! Open the door!

149
10:55.294 --> 10:56.294
Nava, come here.

150
10:58.463 --> 11:01.391
Hey! I said open the door!

151
11:07.572 --> 11:08.078
Hey!

152
11:08.103 --> 11:09.103
Nava.

153
11:09.220 --> 11:11.147
Wait for me. Don’t come out.

154
11:12.080 --> 11:13.275
I said open the door!

155
11:13.299 --> 11:14.299
Trust me, okay?

156
11:21.492 --> 11:23.039
Open the door, or I’ll break in!

157
11:23.343 --> 11:24.343
Metha!

158
11:39.055 --> 11:41.070
Here’s the 10,000 baht you asked for, sir.

159
11:46.959 --> 11:48.986
I came all the way to your house.

160
11:49.609 --> 11:51.055
Aren’t you going to invite me in?

161
11:52.143 --> 11:55.076
I’m hurt, you know.

162
12:05.207 --> 12:06.646
10,000 baht is nothing.

163
12:07.644 --> 12:08.964
How’s that supposed to be enough?

164
12:10.021 --> 12:13.104
You need to get me 100,000.

165
12:13.632 --> 12:14.677
100,000?

166
12:15.998 --> 12:17.256
I only borrowed a million.

167
12:18.387 --> 12:19.944
Only a million?

168
12:20.392 --> 12:23.896
Your debt’s up to three million now.

169
12:26.303 --> 12:27.303
Three million?

170
12:30.166 --> 12:31.446
How did it get to three million?

171
12:31.955 --> 12:33.855
Ever heard of interest?

172
12:35.463 --> 12:37.351
If you can’t pay,

173
12:38.352 --> 12:40.484
you’ll have to pay me another way.

174
12:50.467 --> 12:51.976
What about your daughter?

175
12:53.436 --> 12:57.223
Isn't she going to come out and greet your guests?

176
12:58.220 --> 12:59.916
How rude.

177
13:01.109 --> 13:02.309
Leave my daughter out of this.

178
13:02.394 --> 13:03.394
Get out of my way!

179
13:03.653 --> 13:04.653
Leave her alone.

180
13:05.747 --> 13:06.938
Let go of me!

181
13:08.085 --> 13:09.085
Nava!

182
13:12.027 --> 13:13.497
Open the door for me, sweetheart.

183
13:15.963 --> 13:16.963
Nava.

184
13:17.657 --> 13:18.836
Stay away from my daughter!

185
13:29.291 --> 13:32.406
What can a guy like you do?

186
13:33.115 --> 13:34.763
If you owe me, pay up.

187
13:36.377 --> 13:37.377
Nava!

188
13:37.870 --> 13:39.068
Open the door!

189
13:39.809 --> 13:41.303
Nava!

190
13:41.644 --> 13:42.673
Open the door!

191
13:43.942 --> 13:44.942
You stupid kid!

192
13:45.717 --> 13:47.563
Open the door, you stupid kid!

193
13:55.983 --> 13:57.077
Calm down.

194
13:59.391 --> 14:00.391
Calm down.

195
14:01.743 --> 14:02.743
Get out of my house.

196
14:07.377 --> 14:08.377
Go!

197
14:37.583 --> 14:38.583
Nava.

198
14:43.260 --> 14:44.780
Can you stay with Auntie Jaem tonight?

199
15:23.954 --> 15:25.118
Can I help you?

200
15:31.853 --> 15:32.853
Well...

201
15:34.630 --> 15:37.255
Is it okay if I come back as a night-shift employee?

202
15:37.834 --> 15:38.834
Come on.

203
15:39.326 --> 15:41.529
We’re always happy to welcome back

204
15:42.029 --> 15:44.014
experienced employees.

205
15:44.586 --> 15:45.586
Of course you can.

206
15:49.749 --> 15:52.841
But could I get an advance for the next 10 days?

207
15:57.327 --> 15:58.327
10 days.

208
16:00.147 --> 16:01.444
Yes, well...

209
16:02.833 --> 16:05.233
I need a lot of money for something urgent.

210
16:08.367 --> 16:11.068
I promise I’ll come to work every day.

211
16:11.556 --> 16:12.676
I won’t miss a single shift.

212
16:15.204 --> 16:19.130
And how can you be sure you’ll last the full ten days?

213
16:30.229 --> 16:31.783
I’ll do whatever it takes to survive.

214
16:35.107 --> 16:36.287
Actually,

215
16:38.341 --> 16:40.341
I don’t have the authority to approve this myself.

216
17:04.053 --> 17:05.053
All right.

217
17:05.506 --> 17:06.506
Ten days.

218
17:07.349 --> 17:09.404
I’ll approve the 10-day advance.

219
17:11.748 --> 17:12.748
Really?

220
17:12.873 --> 17:13.873
Yes.

221
17:14.115 --> 17:15.155
Thank you so much.

222
17:16.275 --> 17:19.080
Then work hard,

223
17:19.650 --> 17:22.744
and don’t forget to follow every rule.

224
17:32.361 --> 17:33.361
I will.

225
17:58.017 --> 18:00.399
When did you start working here?

226
18:03.188 --> 18:05.182
Just yesterday.

227
18:05.424 --> 18:06.424
Night shift?

228
18:07.030 --> 18:08.030
Yeah.

229
18:08.611 --> 18:10.284
I want to work the night shift, too.

230
18:10.682 --> 18:12.976
Cherd says it’s always fully staffed.

231
18:14.358 --> 18:15.217
Fully staffed?

232
18:15.339 --> 18:16.339
Yes.

233
18:19.355 --> 18:21.078
Dear.

234
18:22.076 --> 18:23.937
I’m going home.

235
18:24.174 --> 18:25.463
Then go. Who’s stopping you?

236
18:25.995 --> 18:27.554
Aren’t you going to ask me to stay?

237
18:27.633 --> 18:28.225
Nope.

238
18:28.519 --> 18:29.655
You’re so mean.

239
18:33.350 --> 18:35.542
Isn’t Bird coming to work?

240
18:39.476 --> 18:40.828
He won’t be coming back.

241
18:41.985 --> 18:43.040
He’s gone for good.

242
18:48.143 --> 18:49.303
He went back to his hometown?

243
18:50.019 --> 18:51.019
That was sudden.

244
18:54.331 --> 18:55.331
Then...

245
18:55.690 --> 18:57.169
There must be an opening on the night shift now!

246
18:57.193 --> 18:58.574
Then I'll work the night shift.

247
18:58.722 --> 18:59.722
Absolutely not.

248
19:00.460 --> 19:01.724
Why not?

249
19:02.235 --> 19:03.254
You’re annoying.

250
19:04.131 --> 19:05.131
Look.

251
19:05.279 --> 19:07.467
Dear is always picking on me.

252
19:09.739 --> 19:11.019
Because you really are annoying.

253
19:11.342 --> 19:12.992
Finish your work and go home.

254
19:13.049 --> 19:14.209
You’re always kicking me out.

255
19:14.428 --> 19:16.129
It’s late.

256
19:17.414 --> 19:18.414
Are you worried about me?

257
19:18.705 --> 19:20.870
Enough. Go home.

258
19:26.871 --> 19:27.871
Bye.

259
19:40.393 --> 19:44.313
Does what happened to Bird happen often?

260
19:49.772 --> 19:50.772
If they don’t die,

261
19:51.850 --> 19:52.850
they disappear.

262
19:54.654 --> 19:56.254
Some never come back to work.

263
20:00.881 --> 20:01.881
What about you?

264
20:02.161 --> 20:04.519
You quit. Why come back?

265
20:13.328 --> 20:14.448
Or is it just for the money?

266
20:18.601 --> 20:19.601
It’s obvious.

267
20:22.586 --> 20:23.986
Don’t you care about your own life?

268
20:24.372 --> 20:26.169
And you didn’t take this job for the money?

269
20:27.594 --> 20:29.074
Don’t assume everyone’s like you.

270
20:37.063 --> 20:38.352
Go on, get out.

271
20:39.266 --> 20:40.906
Or do you want to watch me get undressed?

272
20:54.375 --> 20:56.453
Inspect deliveries from the delivery truck

273
20:56.478 --> 20:57.478
at the designated time.

274
20:57.734 --> 20:58.734
Rule number 12.

275
20:59.132 --> 21:01.372
Please observe the lights inside this convenience store.

276
21:01.997 --> 21:02.997
Please observe the lights

277
21:03.348 --> 21:05.413
inside the convenience store while on duty.

278
21:05.579 --> 21:09.272
The lights inside the convenience store while on duty.

279
21:10.153 --> 21:11.887
In an emergency,

280
21:12.449 --> 21:15.146
employees may only use the tools provided by the store.

281
21:17.134 --> 21:18.414
The tools provided by the store.

282
21:18.664 --> 21:19.664
Dang it!

283
21:20.311 --> 21:21.311
Can you shut up?

284
21:22.279 --> 21:23.279
You’re annoying.

285
21:24.279 --> 21:25.279
Sorry.

286
21:25.751 --> 21:27.071
I’m afraid I’ll forget the rules.

287
21:29.497 --> 21:31.457
Memorizing the rules doesn’t mean you’ll survive.

288
21:32.387 --> 21:34.015
Those things are crafty.

289
21:40.099 --> 21:42.046
So what exactly are those things?

290
21:54.090 --> 21:56.602
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

291
22:13.868 --> 22:15.527
Would you like a minced pork bun?

292
22:15.655 --> 22:17.303
We have a buy-one-get-one-free promotion.

293
22:30.727 --> 22:32.698
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

294
22:32.723 --> 22:33.964
Please come again.

295
22:40.279 --> 22:42.539
Was that customer... human?

296
22:43.280 --> 22:44.280
Yeah.

297
22:46.762 --> 22:49.756
Then how are we supposed to tell who’s normal?

298
22:51.986 --> 22:53.554
You’ll know when the time comes.

299
22:56.080 --> 22:57.324
If you know anything, tell me.

300
22:58.207 --> 22:59.246
We have to work together.

301
23:02.309 --> 23:03.309
At least...

302
23:05.396 --> 23:07.316
you could show me how to use this cash register.

303
23:19.545 --> 23:20.978
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

304
23:22.458 --> 23:23.505
Are you new here?

305
23:27.558 --> 23:28.558
Yes, I am.

306
23:29.185 --> 23:31.015
I'm here to buy toothpaste,

307
23:32.866 --> 23:34.538
but I don’t know where it is.

308
23:36.083 --> 23:37.083
Young man.

309
23:38.458 --> 23:39.780
Could you help me?

310
23:42.685 --> 23:43.803
The toothpaste is this way.

311
23:44.411 --> 23:45.694
Please follow me.

312
24:03.481 --> 24:04.674
That’ll be 58 baht.

313
24:04.791 --> 24:05.875
We have a special offer.

314
24:05.909 --> 24:08.545
Pair it with a toothpaste for just 60 baht

315
24:08.570 --> 24:09.970
instead of the regular price of 75.

316
24:10.064 --> 24:11.064
Would you like to get it?

317
24:12.610 --> 24:13.790
No, thank you.

318
24:47.351 --> 24:48.524
Five...

319
24:49.278 --> 24:50.278
Six...

320
24:50.658 --> 24:51.658
Fifty-seven.

321
24:54.485 --> 24:55.680
You’re one baht short.

322
24:56.984 --> 24:58.752
Count it again, dear.

323
25:27.023 --> 25:28.110
Fifty-seven.

324
25:28.135 --> 25:29.535
You’re still one baht short, ma'am.

325
26:04.378 --> 26:06.031
Count it again, dear.

326
26:20.203 --> 26:21.234
That’s the full amount.

327
26:28.905 --> 26:30.293
No bag, thank you.

328
26:31.351 --> 26:32.758
Save the planet.

329
26:47.378 --> 26:48.873
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

330
27:02.572 --> 27:03.572
Oh.

331
27:03.978 --> 27:05.658
You know how to use the cash register now.

332
27:05.758 --> 27:07.571
You can work the counter from now on.

333
27:09.332 --> 27:11.045
Just remember to follow the rules.

334
28:01.440 --> 28:02.219
Rule number four.

335
28:02.307 --> 28:03.904
Employees must greet customers, thank them,

336
28:03.928 --> 28:05.991
and inform them of promotions.

337
28:17.378 --> 28:19.260
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

338
28:29.965 --> 28:31.562
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

339
28:31.908 --> 28:32.908
Please come again.

340
28:36.087 --> 28:37.567
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

341
28:38.380 --> 28:39.380
Please come again.

342
28:51.625 --> 28:52.825
Why don’t you use the glasses?

343
28:55.585 --> 28:56.585
What glasses?

344
28:56.618 --> 28:58.016
The store equipment

345
28:59.199 --> 29:00.751
we use in emergencies.

346
29:01.826 --> 29:02.826
These glasses...

347
29:03.043 --> 29:04.697
let night-shift employees like us

348
29:05.222 --> 29:06.997
see the special customers.

349
29:08.599 --> 29:09.599
You didn’t know?

350
29:09.668 --> 29:10.668
I had no idea.

351
29:16.685 --> 29:17.685
What's the matter?

352
29:24.391 --> 29:26.031
Why didn’t you tell me about the glasses?

353
29:26.811 --> 29:28.051
I almost broke a rule just now.

354
29:29.250 --> 29:30.317
You didn’t ask.

355
29:31.011 --> 29:32.550
Besides, I was busy.

356
29:33.121 --> 29:34.448
I was following the rules, too.

357
29:34.667 --> 29:36.200
Do I really have to ask about something that important?

358
29:36.224 --> 29:38.001
You know how dangerous this place is.

359
29:38.026 --> 29:39.026
So what?

360
29:39.640 --> 29:41.460
Do I have to follow you around every second?

361
29:42.688 --> 29:43.890
This isn’t a small matter.

362
29:44.694 --> 29:45.814
People’s lives are at stake.

363
29:48.354 --> 29:50.674
Have you gotten so used to it that you don’t care anymore?

364
29:51.748 --> 29:52.748
Yeah.

365
29:52.812 --> 29:53.812
That’s just how I am.

366
29:54.294 --> 29:55.810
I don't care about anyone.

367
29:55.974 --> 29:57.681
I'm selfish. So what?

368
29:57.706 --> 29:59.434
Shouldn’t you at least have some humanity?

369
29:59.459 --> 30:00.904
You’re the one who keeps thinking

370
30:01.177 --> 30:02.461
someone else will come save you.

371
30:03.108 --> 30:04.634
If you can’t survive on your own,

372
30:05.441 --> 30:06.641
even if I told you everything,

373
30:06.836 --> 30:08.616
you still wouldn’t make it.

374
30:14.645 --> 30:15.738
I’m going to take a break.

375
30:25.791 --> 30:26.791
Dear.

376
30:28.144 --> 30:29.241
You know very well

377
30:30.036 --> 30:32.863
that no one can work the night shift at Sunny Mart alone.

378
30:33.756 --> 30:35.668
If you let something like this happen again,

379
30:37.416 --> 30:38.889
you’ll be the one in trouble.

380
30:44.531 --> 30:45.531
Who knows?

381
30:46.938 --> 30:47.938
Maybe Metha

382
30:48.411 --> 30:50.546
could help solve your problem one day.

383
30:52.254 --> 30:53.254
You never know.

384
30:58.209 --> 31:00.324
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

385
32:27.245 --> 32:28.245
Whoa!

386
33:11.611 --> 33:12.611
Hey, bro.

387
33:13.685 --> 33:14.685
Hey.

388
33:22.251 --> 33:23.851
How long have you been doing this, Good?

389
33:27.037 --> 33:28.239
Oh...

390
33:28.849 --> 33:30.145
So long I’ve lost track, bro.

391
33:31.139 --> 33:32.139
What’s up?

392
33:32.478 --> 33:34.271
Good, do you know what this store really is?

393
33:39.931 --> 33:41.007
I’m not really sure.

394
33:43.559 --> 33:45.658
I just know the pay’s good, so people give it a try.

395
33:46.798 --> 33:47.798
But...

396
33:47.869 --> 33:49.133
they never last long.

397
33:56.031 --> 33:57.569
Has anyone stayed for a long time?

398
33:58.178 --> 33:59.220
People don’t stick around.

399
34:00.713 --> 34:01.713
If you don’t count Cherd,

400
34:01.936 --> 34:03.643
the one who’s been here the longest is

401
34:04.010 --> 34:05.010
Dear.

402
34:05.637 --> 34:06.797
It’s been about three months.

403
34:08.363 --> 34:09.363
Three months?

404
34:09.730 --> 34:10.730
Yeah.

405
34:11.236 --> 34:12.534
Most people come and go.

406
34:13.410 --> 34:14.410
They...

407
34:14.441 --> 34:16.504
they say they can’t handle the customers.

408
34:21.723 --> 34:22.723
Good.

409
34:24.556 --> 34:26.161
What exactly are these customers?

410
34:26.916 --> 34:27.916
Ghosts?

411
34:28.341 --> 34:29.341
Spirits?

412
34:41.198 --> 34:42.563
It doesn't matter what they are.

413
34:45.358 --> 34:46.358
One thing’s for sure.

414
34:47.005 --> 34:48.147
They can kill you.

415
34:52.358 --> 34:53.731
They’re just waiting for a chance.

416
34:54.811 --> 34:56.132
Waiting for you to make a mistake.

417
34:56.156 --> 34:57.156
Just once.

418
35:03.011 --> 35:05.553
If you see anything strange, just follow the rules.

419
35:10.251 --> 35:11.785
Oh, and...

420
35:14.081 --> 35:16.681
Don’t trust anything that looks too much like a person.

421
35:39.403 --> 35:40.403
Here. Take the glasses.

422
35:42.631 --> 35:43.254
No, thanks.

423
35:43.583 --> 35:45.023
I thought you said it was essential.

424
35:50.044 --> 35:51.913
Don’t I have to survive on my own?

425
35:55.991 --> 35:56.991
Suit yourself.

426
35:57.771 --> 35:59.031
Just don’t blame me later.

427
36:02.804 --> 36:04.874
Hello, welcome to Sunny Mart.

428
36:10.764 --> 36:11.667
Rule number 12.

429
36:11.692 --> 36:13.514
When the lights turn green,

430
36:13.584 --> 36:14.862
employees must never make eye contact

431
36:14.886 --> 36:16.654
with customers who enter the store.

432
36:24.478 --> 36:27.111
I want betel nut... and betel leaves...

433
36:29.739 --> 36:31.958
I want betel nut and betel leaves.

434
36:38.021 --> 36:40.463
I want betel nut and betel leaves.

435
36:45.261 --> 36:46.261
Just a moment, sir.

436
36:53.891 --> 36:55.691
The betel nut and leaves are in this section.

437
36:56.010 --> 36:57.284
Please follow me.

438
37:05.099 --> 37:06.099
Dear.

439
37:08.371 --> 37:09.371
Dear, help me!

440
37:13.576 --> 37:14.576
Dear!

441
37:19.838 --> 37:20.838
Help me!

442
37:39.851 --> 37:40.851
This way, sir.

443
38:09.044 --> 38:10.044
Where is it?

444
38:11.638 --> 38:12.638
Where is it?

445
38:14.571 --> 38:15.728
Please wait a moment, sir.

446
39:15.657 --> 39:16.657
Dear!

447
39:20.671 --> 39:21.671
Dear!

448
39:24.812 --> 39:25.812
Dear, are you here?

449
40:09.164 --> 40:10.164
Dear!

450
40:11.364 --> 40:12.364
Keep quiet.

451
40:15.056 --> 40:16.056
But...

452
40:19.091 --> 40:21.184
I knew I’d find you here sooner or later.

453
40:21.851 --> 40:22.891
We’re getting out of here.

454
40:23.791 --> 40:25.106
Come on. Let’s go.

455
40:25.851 --> 40:26.851
There you are.

456
40:28.801 --> 40:29.801
Who’s that?

457
40:33.589 --> 40:34.589
This is my brother.

458
40:35.309 --> 40:36.942
I won’t let them take him.

459
40:39.123 --> 40:40.123
No.

460
40:40.443 --> 40:41.763
You have to return him to them right now.

461
40:41.787 --> 40:43.650
No! What would you know?

462
40:44.534 --> 40:45.534
Come on, Den.

463
40:47.254 --> 40:48.587
What’s your problem?

464
40:50.114 --> 40:51.158
I'm taking Den away.

465
40:51.183 --> 40:52.183
Dear.

466
40:54.453 --> 40:55.614
That's not your brother.

467
41:35.219 --> 41:36.219
Dear!

468
41:40.008 --> 41:41.008
Dear.

469
42:04.851 --> 42:06.818
Thank you for shopping at Sunny Mart.

470
42:17.707 --> 42:19.476
Every time the lights turn green,

471
42:20.194 --> 42:22.740
this customer comes into the store carrying a sack.

472
42:23.101 --> 42:24.154
And inside that sack,

473
42:24.721 --> 42:26.010
it takes the form of someone

474
42:26.478 --> 42:27.478
we’re thinking about,

475
42:27.718 --> 42:28.718
to lure its victims.

476
42:31.338 --> 42:32.338
Just now,

477
42:33.045 --> 42:34.525
If Metha hadn’t helped,

478
42:34.787 --> 42:36.497
Dear would’ve been caught in the sack

479
42:36.867 --> 42:38.388
and become its replacement victim.

480
42:41.994 --> 42:42.994
These things...

481
42:43.380 --> 42:45.180
They’re not just coming in to shop, are they?

482
42:45.674 --> 42:48.090
They seem to be deliberately choosing people.

483
42:48.747 --> 42:50.227
Each one has its own way of doing it.

484
42:50.920 --> 42:51.920
That’s right.

485
42:52.941 --> 42:53.941
That’s why

486
42:54.339 --> 42:56.285
our employees have to look out for one another,

487
42:57.996 --> 42:59.082
so no one

488
43:00.464 --> 43:01.464
breaks the rules.

489
43:05.798 --> 43:06.798
But for now...

490
43:11.468 --> 43:13.492
we’d better clean up this store.

491
43:15.865 --> 43:16.898
It’s a complete mess.

492
43:18.159 --> 43:19.159
The morning shift staff

493
43:21.751 --> 43:22.981
will be shocked.

494
43:39.384 --> 43:40.584
About what happened earlier...

495
43:43.718 --> 43:44.718
Thanks.

496
43:46.011 --> 43:47.011
It’s nothing.

497
43:53.198 --> 43:54.198
What’s that?

498
43:55.371 --> 43:56.791
Do you have Instagram?

499
44:00.370 --> 44:02.476
If not, your phone number will do.

500
44:29.971 --> 44:30.971
I’m heading out.

501
44:34.958 --> 44:35.958
Yeah.

502
45:01.338 --> 45:06.324
(Help me!)

503
45:11.906 --> 45:12.539
What's this?

504
45:12.702 --> 45:13.398
I got it for you.

505
45:13.593 --> 45:14.953
Have you always lived alone, Dear?

506
45:15.080 --> 45:16.429
That must get lonely.

507
45:17.091 --> 45:18.091
Don’t worry.

508
45:18.156 --> 45:19.312
I don’t think anything will happen tonight.

509
45:19.336 --> 45:20.576
It’s the quiet nights like this

510
45:22.176 --> 45:23.176
that are scarier.

511
45:28.724 --> 45:29.724
You two!

512
45:30.016 --> 45:31.282
Get away from the counter!

513
45:31.469 --> 45:32.469
Store rule.

514
45:33.171 --> 45:33.989
The counter must not be left unattended

515
45:34.013 --> 45:35.039
for more than three minutes.

516
45:35.063 --> 45:36.641
I don’t care about your stupid rules!

517
45:36.750 --> 45:38.367
Is this really all there is?
